*
* START-HISTORY:
* 22 Oct 26 dm  New (S.75; the owner: "if defined by the admin or the system, it should be able to be turned off by the admin", then "disabling tiles should be on a
*               per account basis, by default they are on").
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call !home_off(account, off)
*
*     account  the account's name
*     off      returned: the ids of the tiles that are off for it, in lower case, separated by single spaces (null when none): the words of field 17 of the account's
*              register record (SET.TILE account tile off)
*
*   Tiles are ON as delivered and are turned off one account at a time; there is no list for every account.  Read-only, for the home screen (which leaves those
*   tiles out), !HOME_ENTRY (an account whose Terminal tile is off is not given the prompt) and SET.TILE.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine home_off(acct, off)
$catalog !home_off

$include keys.h

   off = ''
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'accounts' to af then
      read arec from af, downcase(acct) then off = arec<ACC$TILES.OFF>
      close af
   end
   off = downcase(trim(convert(',' : char(9), '  ', off)))

   return
end

* END-CODE
